id=resolve-reblock
class=state
found=the review behind 1.1.16, 2026-10-11
fixed=1.1.16
test=test/26_resolve_reblock.sql
detail=lock_tree_notify_resolved() read the live tree twice: a SELECT chose what to report cleared
       and a separate DELETE chose what to forget. A root that started blocking again between the
       two was reported cleared and its alert row was kept, so the next lock_tree_notify() treated
       it as already alerted and sent nothing for an incident still under way. test/26
       re-establishes the incident from a shadowed pg_notify while the resolver is between the two
       statements; the one-statement DELETE ... RETURNING forgets the row exactly when it reports
       it, and the two-statement version keeps it.
